WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.720
Hey, Daigo! How long are you
going to spend in that bathroom?

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:07.190
The Summer Tournament Begins!

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.400
The team bus is here.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.150
I'm really sorry about this, Mutsuko-chan.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.200
It's fine.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.200
Is your stomach acting up again?

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.460
This happens every time 
you take part in some event.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.520
Are you okay?

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.980
I'm fine. I'm fine.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.410
I'm empty now, pretty much.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.170
Uh, what are you doing?

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.460
Oh, you know!

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.490
We have a match soon and all...

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.540
Good luck!

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.640
I'll be on the sidelines, cheering for you!

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:39.370
Right.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.980
Then, I'm off!

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.220
<i>We're finally underway.</i>

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.910
<i>Kanagawa's prelims for 
the National Tournament!</i>

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:25.370
All right.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:28.200
I'm going to announce our starting lineup.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.100
Yes, sir!

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:31.890
Batting first, shortstop, Kimura.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:32.660
Yes, sir!

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.630
Batting second, right field,

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:37.630
Shigeno.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.610
I-I'm second in the order?

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.560
Batting third, pitcher, Urabe!

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:47.000
Yep.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:50.810
Batting fourth, catcher, Andy.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:51.600
Yes, sir.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.700
Batting fifth, third base, Ariyoshi.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:54.620
Yes, sir!

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.550
Batting sixth, left field, Kishimoto.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:57.360
Yes, sir!

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:59.680
Batting seventh, first base, Matsubara.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:00.670
Yes, sir!

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:02.560
Batting eighth, center field, Nagai.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.380
Yes, sir!

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.360
Batting ninth, second base, Katsumoto.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:05.990
Yes, sir!

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:09.110
The subs are Tsuburaya, 
Takahashi, and Sakura.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.210
That's everything.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:14.960
Manager...

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.430
I usually bat second.
How come I'm eighth this time?

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.100
Sorry, Nagai.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.840
Based on his performances lately, 
I've decided to swap you and Shigeno.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.380
Dolphins, please start your warm-up.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.730
Yes, sir!

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.440
U-Uh, Manager...

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:37.380
You said I've performed well recently,
but I can't suddenly hit top of the order.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.940
Have faith in yourself, Daigo!

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:43.680
In the last two weeks, your fitness and 
technique have come on leaps and bounds.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:44.980
I can tell.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.560
And the other day, I had it confirmed
that I wasn't just imagining it.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:51.310
Huh?

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.300
You had him as your coach, 
and you've been training every day.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:58.540
Don't worry.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.700
Satou-san told us he's confident 
you'll do just fine in the two hole.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:04.640
<i>He said that?</i>

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.360
Keep calm and play on.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:48.720
That you're still registered as part 
of their team for the tournament.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:51.420
According to the rules,

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.350
you can play in the matches as a member
of the Dolphins, no matter where you live.

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:57.680
R-Really?!

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:01.720
I can really play in the tournament?

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:02.670
Yup.

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:05.200
Manager Tashiro said you 
should definitely go, too.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:08.910
But I'm not going to.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.880
By now, I'm an outsider...

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:16.260
It's not like I trained for very long
with the team.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.940
It wouldn't sit right if I just 
turned up for the tournament.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.850
Nobody... wants that.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.820
<i>Guess he really didn't come.</i>

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.600
Line up.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.380
Let's do this!

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.360
A lefty. Not much more to say.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.650
Yeah, his pitches are nothing special.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:52.890
<i>The two hole, huh?</i>

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.330
<i>I've never had the chance to hit
in the very first inning before.</i>

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.640
<i>My stomach's okay, too.</i>

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.090
<i>All right!</i>

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.050
<i>All I have to do now is show off 
what I've been practicing.</i>

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.240
Play ball!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:17.810
Strike.

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:22.930
I can't even begin to imagine how 
you greased Manager's palms this time.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:25.900
Ball.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.400
First, right field, and now the two hole?

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:33.370
Damn, wish I'd been born 
the son of a rich baseball player.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:34.780
This again?

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:36.480
Give it a rest.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:41.380
I haven't done anything, and the manager
wouldn't let us influence his lineups.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.130
I wonder.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:48.300
I'm saying that if I were manager
and saw your folks donate that bus,

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.800
even I would feel obliged to
put you in the starting lineup.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.370
It got through!

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:01.560
Awesome! A double!

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.480
Nice! No outs, and a runner on second!

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.030
This is our chance to pull ahead!

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.280
We're counting on you, Daigo!

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.750
You got this, Shigeno-kun!

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.500
I really would like to take the lead here.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:19.830
If we can get the runner to third,
Urabe or Andy will bring him home for sure.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:23.310
<i>Bunt, Daigo.</i>

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:27.900
Play!

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.260
Hey, Daigo!

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:31.680
What the hell? He's not 
watching for our signs!

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:31.970
Huh?

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:34.470
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:37.470
<i>Stop saying I'm riding 
on Pop's coattails!</i>

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:39.460
<i>Right...</i>

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:43.400
<i>I'll show you that I'm a regular on merit!</i>

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.140
Foul!

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:55.920
Timeout!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:00.620
You idiot!

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:02.330
E-Excuse me?

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:03.890
Didn't you see my sign?

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:04.580
Huh?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.380
I gave you the signal for a sacrifice bunt!

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.840
Huh? Ah, sorry.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.320
Pull yourself together.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.600
Y-Yes, sir.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:14.340
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:17.220
<i>I was so angry at Urabe that 
I ignored instructions.</i>

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.640
<i>That wasn't the time to 
take a swing at the ball.</i>

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.560
<i>Another sacrifice bunt.</i>

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:29.520
Play.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:35.100
When the runner's on second,

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.990
<i>the bunt has to be a bit stronger, 
so the third baseman has to run to get it.</i>

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.120
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:44.190
He missed?!

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.250
Kimura, get back!

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:47.760
Seriously?!

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:49.350
Safe!

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:50.550
That was close.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:55.510
See, I told you. It's too soon 
to put Daigo in at second.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.470
He's got two strikes against him.
 Just let him swing.

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:02.180
What?!

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:03.930
<i>Another bunt?!</i>

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:07.870
If I was going to lose faith so easily,
I wouldn't have put him in the two hole.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:11.510
I made my decision because
 I believe Daigo's up for the task.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:17.280
If my plan fails, I'll just have to 
apologize to Daigo and the team.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.580
Play!

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:28.380
<i>Manager believes in me.</i>

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:33.080
<i>I'm not riding on Pop's coattails.</i>

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:37.350
<i>He's put me in the two hole because 
he's seen how I've engaged with baseball.</i>

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.500
<i>Hey, now...</i>

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:43.890
<i>You didn't even touch the last one, 
and you're bunting with one strike left?</i>

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:51.400
Ball!

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:56.400
<i>Yup. He's calmed down now.</i>

00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:58.360
<i>That's it.</i>

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:02.410
<i>You've been tracking a lot of pitches 
with your eyes and your body.</i>

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:06.140
<i>All you've done is swapped the mitt for a bat.</i>

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.800
<i>All these balls should 
be child's play for you.</i>

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:16.300
He did it!

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:18.720
Third!

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.710
Wait! Let it go! If it's a foul, he's out!

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:24.280
Huh?

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:30.520
It's a foul!

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:31.750
Fair!

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:32.920
All right!

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.530
It touched the base before 
going out, so it's a fair ball!

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:36.250
All right!

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.160
That was close.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.730
Sweet! He made it to first, too!

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:40.120
No outs, runners on first and third!

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:41.530
Nice, Shigeno-kun!

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.490
<i>Whew, what a relief.</i>

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:47.520
<i>He was living life on the edge, 
but all in all, a nice bunt.</i>

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:49.450
Oh, Satou-san!

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:50.610
Oh, hello.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.460
You're here, too?

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:56.190
You've already missed 
Daigo-kun's first at bat.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.540
He's batting second today.

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:58.390
What?

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:02.680
His sacrifice bunt turned into 
a regular hit, and he made it on base.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:06.200
Really? Not bad, Daigo!

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:07.880
Play!

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:12.720
<i>Hmph. A lucky hit and he starts fist-pumping?</i>

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:14.130
<i>Talk about "suck-ond" generation.</i>

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:17.150
<i>I'll show you what a first-generation 
genius can do with a bat.</i>

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:22.080
<i>On the first pitch, there's no chance 
for a squeeze or a hit-and-run.</i>

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:25.880
<i>The other team is geared up 
to stop us getting any runners home.</i>

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:34.460
<i>Huh?</i>

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.210
What?!

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:38.670
What the hell is he doing?!

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.090
<i>Oh, crap!</i>

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.550
Oh, boy.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:47.560
I didn't teach him to watch out 
for pickoffs by lefty pitchers.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:51.890
<i>I have no choice but to make a run for second!</i>

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:56.230
<i>And back!</i>

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:58.440
<i>It's over!</i>

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.320
Home!

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.770
Back home!

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.030
<i>I'm not going to make it.</i>

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:07.530
Safe!

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:08.620
All right!

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.000
We took the lead!

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.440
Nice running, Kimura!

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:13.500
Kimura, nice running!

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:16.130
What?!

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:18.960
Why isn't that idiot on second base?!

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.640
"Idiot"? Huh?

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.130
Oh.

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.560
Sheesh, what's that kid doing?

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:27.020
Baserunning's all about experience.

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:29.420
The kid who made it home 
has matches under his belt,

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:30.970
and made a good call.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.950
But wasn't it quite a risky steal?

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:36.730
In junior baseball, the kids 
make plenty of mistakes.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:39.400
In general, risky plays are fine.

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:40.840
Play!

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:43.900
<i>I'll stay closer to the base this time.</i>

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.200
<i>That moron.</i>

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:49.190
<i>He ruined my chance to bring a runner home.</i>

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:53.910
<i>Sticking that loser second in the order... 
I bet Manager really </i>was<i> bribed!</i>

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.290
All right, good hit into center field.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:12:59.290
Nice!

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:01.940
Second!

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:08.330
Out!

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:11.100
Thrown out from center field?

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:15.830
No way.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:19.340
Because of his mistake earlier, 
he stood closer to his base.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:21.610
And he didn't get a very good jump, either.

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.450
IQ, you know? It's about IQ.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:30.170
Get it into your skull already. 
You have no baseball IQ.

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:32.200
Just tell 'em you twisted your ankle

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:35.210
and sit out the rest of the game
on the bench, rich boy.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:38.310
Before you cause even more 
trouble for the team.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:42.510
Play!

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.560
<i>Shigeno-kun...</i>

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:55.740
Out!

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:58.020
Out!

00:13:58.210 --> 00:13:59.640
Three outs! Change sides!

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:01.250
Ah, man! A double play!

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.020
Aw.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.030
Mifune

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.030
Tanikawa

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.020
So we only scored one run in the end.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:07.570
If only Daigo hadn't made a hash of it...

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:09.650
It's only the first inning.

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:13.120
There's still plenty of chances 
for Daigo-kun to turn things around.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.140
Let's go, defense!

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:17.110
Sakura!

00:14:17.110 --> 00:14:17.790
Yes?

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:22.600
<i>I've really done it now.</i>

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:25.430
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.120
<i>The only thing I pulled off 
was that sacrifice bunt.</i>

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:33.480
<i>I missed signs, got caught out by a pickoff
attempt, and got thrown out from center.</i>

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.810
<i>Maybe I really don't have any baseball IQ.</i>

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:38.810
Shigeno-kun!

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:46.280
<i>Of course. I'm being switched out.</i>

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.740
Okay, I'll leave the rest to you.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.660
Huh? Where are you going?

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:53.620
Your hat, your hat!

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.840
Manager asked if you were gonna
field wearing your helmet.

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:56.370
Oh!

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:58.370
I'm not being swapped out?

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.430
Swapped out? For me?

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:01.660
What are you talking about?

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:04.380
Of course not! It's only the first inning.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.880
But, I mean, I screwed up so much...

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:09.120
What? You want to be swapped out?

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:10.430
I'll take your place.

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:11.640
I want to play, too.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.320
N-No, I'll play.

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:22.740
Oh, yeah, message from Manager.

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:26.200
"Make as many mistakes as you like.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:29.480
But if I see any halfhearted plays 
because you're afraid of messing up,

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:31.990
you'll be out in a heartbeat," he says!

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:59.910
<i>What's important is to not
dwell on your mistakes.</i>

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:02.560
Play!

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.630
Right!

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:18.660
<i>It's true.</i>

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:22.180
<i>I never had any baseball IQ.</i>

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:26.740
Out!

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:32.310
<i>All I need to do is go after the balls!</i>

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.020
Mifune

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.020
Tanikawa

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.620
This is our chance!

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:49.270
Knock it out of the park, Shigeno-kun!

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:58.450
Strike! Batter out!

00:16:58.860 --> 00:16:59.700
Change sides!

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:16.970
What do <i>you</i> want?

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:21.540
Sorry! Next time, 
I'll definitely make it count!

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:24.480
Let's banish it from our minds. 
I'm counting on you and your pitches!

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.650
What makes you think
you can say that to me?

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:35.200
Trash like you shouldn't be touching 
my golden right shoulder.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.210
Here you go.

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:41.910
Thanks.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:48.850
<i>I'm not gonna let every 
little detail get me down.</i>

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:50.920
<i>I need to just focus on the next play.</i>

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.920
Mifune

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.920
Tanikawa

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:56.420
<i>Well, I'm pitching a perfect game so far.</i>

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:58.920
<i>At this rate, against this team,</i>

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:01.600
<i>one run should be plenty!</i>

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.140
Strike! Out!

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:06.640
Batter out!

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.650
Out! Change sides!

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:11.540
Nice pitching, Urabe!

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:14.820
Don't you think you're overdoing it?

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.660
If you try to protect our 
one-run lead at all costs,

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:20.100
you'll be exhausted by the later innings.

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:22.620
Nah, I'm only throwing at
70 per cent right now.

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:24.870
Anyway, let's go get some more runs.

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:31.330
<i>Following Urabe's hit and Andy's double,
we had runners on second and third.</i>

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:35.430
<i>It was a great chance,
but now we're on two outs.</i>

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:40.550
Letting this kind of opportunity go begging 
shifts the momentum to the other team.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.220
Go, Matsubara!

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:43.180
Please hit it.

00:18:47.170 --> 00:18:47.680
Out!

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:51.690
<i>Damn it. No matter how well 
Andy and I hit, the rest can't follow up.</i>

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:54.440
Guess I can't bank on us 
getting any more runs.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:56.440
Mifune

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:56.440
Tanikawa

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:59.240
<i>So I've got no choice 
but to protect our lead.</i>

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.340
Ack, they finally got a runner.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:14.960
S-Sorry! My bad.

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:18.160
<i>Damn it. I had a perfect game going.</i>

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:20.370
<i>Guess I can't get one with this defense.</i>

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:22.680
<i>At least I'm still throwing a no-hitter.</i>

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:29.310
<i>Sweet. That one's in the bag.</i>

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:32.500
Got it!

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.590
Got it!

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:35.940
What?!

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:39.110
Who says "got it" and lets it go?!

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:40.390
Yeah! Our first hit!

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:41.890
One out, runners on first and second!

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:43.930
This is our chance to catch up!

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:45.980
<i>How did that turn into a hit?</i>

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:48.330
<i>The way he hit it, he's getting 
caught out all day long!</i>

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:53.560
Play!

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:56.290
<i>Guess this game's going 
the same way as all the rest.</i>

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:00.470
Ball!

00:20:00.940 --> 00:20:01.760
Ball!

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:02.800
Ball!

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:05.390
Ball!

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:06.410
Ball four!

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:08.100
Yes! Bases loaded!

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:12.780
Oh dear, that's bad.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:14.600
They're in a tight spot.

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:17.570
Timeout, please.

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:19.030
Damn it!

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.420
Don't sweat it. Calm down, Urabe.

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:23.170
I know!

00:20:23.170 --> 00:20:27.030
I know, but it's pissing me off
how bad our defense still is!

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:30.320
And there I was, pitching a perfect game!

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:33.780
Maybe you haven't improved 
as much as you think, either.

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:35.040
What?

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:39.020
Up to now, you've always gone to pieces 
when your teammates have made errors.

00:20:39.020 --> 00:20:41.320
You want to continue the pattern
and lose again?

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:48.800
Remember why we joined 
Mifune in the first place.

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:51.500
Blaming our teammates won't get us anywhere.

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:00.720
What? You're quitting the Touto Boys?

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:01.230
Yes.

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.580
But why, Tobecchi?

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:07.350
We promised each other 
we'd always play baseball together.

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:10.570
I'm sorry, but it's not like 
I'm quitting baseball altogether.

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:12.100
I'm joining my local team, the Dolphins.

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:13.660
Huh? Why?

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:16.060
The Dolphins are ultra weak right now.

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:19.330
If you play for them, you'll never 
win and it'll suck big time.

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:22.800
I know that.

00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:25.640
But I can't keep playing for the Touto Boys.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:29.180
As long as <i>he's</i> there, 
I'll never be the ace.

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:32.520
I want to join another team and defeat him.

00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:36.060
Oh, so that's why.

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:38.020
Then, I'll come with you to the Dolphins.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.020
Huh?

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:44.250
<i>We made a promise back then, didn't we?</i>

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:46.930
<i>That we'd always play baseball together.</i>

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:00.200
Fly ball, right field!

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:02.080
All right! A sacrifice fly!

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:03.550
Amazing! That means we're even!

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:05.140
<i>They got us.</i>

00:22:05.140 --> 00:22:07.800
<i>Of </i>course<i> they'd send it out 
to the guy with the weak arm.</i>

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:08.980
<i>Bastards!</i>

00:22:08.980 --> 00:22:12.510
<i>This is why I was against 
making that loser a regular!</i>

00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:15.590
Here it is. His time to shine.

00:22:15.590 --> 00:22:16.350
Huh?

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:18.520
Go!

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:22.480
Please watch how much he has grown.

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:02.740
The Dolphins are in the lead.

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:07.130
But up to now, it's essentially been only 
Andy and Urabe who've done anything.

00:24:07.530 --> 00:24:11.590
Seems like Urabe's getting tired, 
so the defense needs to stay sharp!

00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:16.680
Just watch. I'll show you the fruits 
of my training with Satou-san!

00:24:17.620 --> 00:24:20.140
Next time: "Now I've Done It!"

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
Now I've Done It!

00:24:20.530 --> 00:24:22.560
Run to the stage of your dreams!
